  "lineage": "Late-1980s-and-1990s heavy-metal-and-rock subgenre developed primarily in California (Palm Desert \"desert rock\" scene) and northern Europe, characterized by down-tuned-distorted guitar tone, slow-to-mid-tempo grooves, vintage-1970s-Sabbath-Hendrix sonic reference, and improvisational-jam-oriented composition. Kyuss (Palm Desert, 1987-1995) and Sleep (San Jose, 1990-1998) inaugurated the canonical American sound; Queens of the Stone Age (1996-onward, Kyuss successor) extended the genre commercially.",
